From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:31:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: hci_bcm: retry the baud rate change after a reset

On the Pixel 6 Pro (BCM4389C1 on the APM UART) the controller sometimes
ignores the 0xfc18 baud rate change that follows the first HCI_Reset
after power-on: 0xfc18 times out, while another HCI_Reset and Read Local
Version are answered at 115200. The firmware download then runs at
115200, and the HCI command timer fires on Launch RAM, so the
controller never comes up.

When 0xfc18 times out, send HCI_Reset and, if it is answered, retry the
baud rate change once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: saiththerobo <the.tom.sharp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
index facbe96c3..53825ca7b 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_bcm.c
@@ -213,6 +213,23 @@ static int bcm_set_baudrate(struct hci_uart *hu, unsigned int speed)
 	 */
 	skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, 0xfc18, sizeof(param), &param,
 			     HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
+	if (PTR_ERR_OR_ZERO(skb) == -ETIMEDOUT) {
+		/* The BCM4389 can ignore the baud rate change that follows
+		 * the first HCI_Reset after power-on, and still answer a
+		 * second HCI_Reset. Without the baud rate change the firmware
+		 * download runs at the init speed and Launch RAM times out,
+		 * so reset and try once more.
+		 */
+		bt_dev_warn(hdev, "BCM: baud rate change timed out, retrying after reset");
+		skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, HCI_OP_RESET, 0, NULL,
+				     HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
+		if (!IS_ERR(skb)) {
+			kfree_skb(skb);
+			msleep(100);
+			skb = __hci_cmd_sync(hdev, 0xfc18, sizeof(param),
+					     &param, HCI_INIT_TIMEOUT);
+		}
+	}
 	if (IS_ERR(skb)) {
 		int err = PTR_ERR(skb);
 		bt_dev_err(hdev, "BCM: failed to write update baudrate (%d)",
